  "brief": "Abandoned two-storey frame folk I-house, rectangular plan with a side-gable roof of plain corrugated metal, silvered unpainted lap siding and simple corner pilasters. Windows boarded with plywood; the front porch is gone, leaving only four rock-faced limestone piers and a ledger line across the facade. The ruin of a one-storey rear kitchen addition sags off the back; a flagstone walk still leads through tall grass. The family moved to town and rents out the ground.",
